liable, creates positive atmosphere with crew. D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership.\n\nWe need to discuss candidate B's crew cooperation concerns (uncooperative, grumpy). Also candidate C is 100% reliable and creates positive atmosphere, but communication difficulty. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWe could argue that candidate C's reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh communication issues? Or that candidate D's responsibility and problem solving are strong, but arrogance is concerning.\n\nWe need to decide whether to keep vote B or shift. Perhaps we can ask James about stress resilience for A or D. But we can also give our own assessment: B's strengths are strong, but concerns about uncooperative behavior could be serious for crew. C's reliability and positive crew atmosphere might be better overall. However C's egocentric and communication difficulty may affect safety. D's responsibility and problem solving are strong, but arrogance and weak leadership may be problematic.\n\nGiven the evidence, B still seems best. We can support Emily's recommendation, but note concerns about B's uncooperative behavior and suggest we need more info on D's stress handling. But we can keep vote B.\n\nThus public message: agree with Emily, highlight B's strengths, note concerns, but still recommend B. Provide explicit facts. Provide reasoning.\n\nLet's produce."}
